  "findings": [
    "All ten supplied cases visibly/native-observably acquire NODE_OT_link and end that handler after their terminal event.",
    "Fresh Finish creates SourceA.Value to SinkB.Value; actual native Undo removes it and Redo restores the same valid endpoint tuple.",
    "Fresh empty release opens the native linked-node search popup, then Esc discards it; graph endpoints remain empty.",
    "Existing-input acquisition detaches its original link. Empty Finish removes it; native Undo restores and Redo removes it.",
    "Existing-input Esc and RMB cancel end the native handler while leaving the detached link absent. This is observed native behavior and is not asserted to be a user-facing rollback defect.",
    "Returning to the original input with a final MOUSEMOVE restores its valid endpoint tuple; merely releasing at that input after empty-space motion leaves it absent, supporting no release-position repick in this corridor.",
    "Existing-input rewire creates SinkB.Value_001; native Undo restores Value and Redo reapplies Value_001."
  ],
